{"seq":19,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/claude-code-opus-no-style-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T07:26:04.239Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"f9c5d658e9545b7b73d9488a0abfdf96349d7ce0c077b89993a18bd51c1baec7","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent them to you in our DM. Both come from public digests in the team-north folder.\n\n- **#PD-4492**: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (dated 5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their dock door assignments by SMS from the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it the same evening. The note also says the kiosk logs were to be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n- **#4419**: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\", which has no date. Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for firmware testing.\n\nI also checked these places and found no other QFL ticket numbers:\n- **Moss's other two North digests** (14 Sep 2025 and 23 Mar 2026) mention the account but give no ticket numbers.\n- **The ticket numbers in the Central digests** (#4409, #4412, FR-882) are for Marrow accounts, not QFL.\n- **#general and #help-it-ops** have no posts from Moss.\n\nThe cheat sheet also warns that Quarendon Freightways, spelled with one \"r\", is a different company and not a customer, so keep the two apart in the weekly notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
